Refuse, on wasip1, the New Relic CLI commands that install or run native
programs on the machine.

Reason: newrelic install downloads install recipes and runs them (shell
scripts through mvdan.cc/sh, the package manager, sudo) to put agents and
integrations on the machine it runs on, none of which a WASI command can
do.
newrelic diagnose run, update and lint download New Relic Diagnostics
(nrdiag) for linux, darwin or windows into ~/.newrelic/bin and start it.
On wasip1 these stop before any request with their reason; install
refuses before it asks for an API key. --help still works, and so does
newrelic diagnose validate, which only sends an event and queries it.

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: a WASI command can install and start native programs.

